e extractor\nregistered (gate passed) · `partial` = some sibling fields registered · `gap` = nothing registered (TARGET name given\nwhen one exists but is not built yet).\n**Tools:** (I) = installed (`.venv/bin/python` import or on the `source bin/env.sh` PATH), (M) = missing.\nIn-window extractors may only import the prebuild gate's `ALLOWED_IMPORTS` (`hctf/prebuild.py:112`: stdlib subset +\n`pefile elftools capstone Crypto androguard pyzipper lib`) and may NOT call `open()` -- so Evtx / regipy / olefile /\noletools / dnfile / LnkParse3 / lief / cryptography / asn1crypto / dpkt / PIL / `sqlite3` / `mailbox` / `wave` are\nworker-only (LLM side) until the allowlist is widened. See gaps `gate-allowlist-*`.\n**Likelihood** reasoning: D9-D15 walked Windows binaries/installers/shortcuts/Office (PE -> PE version -> .NET -> MSI\n-> LNK -> OOXML); the next steps are most plausibly other Windows DFIR artifacts and legacy-Office/CFB siblings,\nplus deeper fields of already-seen families (timed kits are cumulative, D15 added cross-file synthesis).\n**D16 turned to e-mail** (`email.message_id` of one `.eml`; flavor \"replies, forwards, duplicates, reconstructed\nmessages ... stable message identities\"). PE stayed three days (D9-11) with a deeper field each day, so D17-D19 most\nplausibly ask deeper `email.*` fields (In-Reply-To / References / attachments / Received / auth) or a sibling mail\ncontainer (MBOX, Outlook MSG), then cross-message threading as a synthesis question. GM fmt word is `email`, not `eml`.\n**D17 jumped to audio instead** (`media.primary_audio_codec_name` of one PCM `.wav` -> `pcm_s16le`; id\n`d17-audio-001-media-...`: family `audio`, fmt `media`, ffprobe vocabulary). Flavor: \"Voice notes have been\ntranscoded, renamed, and embedded in mail. Determine the actual codecs, connect equivalent recordings, and find the\nstream that breaks the sender's story.\" -> D18-D20 most plausibly: the same `media.*` namespace on OTHER containers/\ncodecs (renamed `.wav` that is MP3/Ogg-Opus/M4A/AMR -- \"actual codecs\"), deeper ffprobe stream fields (sample_rate,\nchannels, duration, bit_rate, format_name, stream count), a multi-stream container where one stream disagrees\n(\"stream that breaks the story\": language/creation_time/encoder/codec), audio as a MIME attachment inside `.eml`\n(\"embedded in mail\" -- D16 + D17 combined), and a cross-recording equivalence synthesis (\"connect equivalent\nrecordings\": same INFO title / correlation id / PCM payload / duration). Video `media.*` (h264 etc.) is the next step\nafter that. Email fields remain warm (D16 family carries over in every timed kit).\n**D17 post-run:** single/TT/Mastery all asked only `pcm_s16le` (no transcode actually delivered) + the kit + synthesis.\nThe D17-night prebuild covered the whole audio flavor (fmt `media`/`audio`/`av`: codec/stream/format/tags/odd-stream,\n`email.attachment_audio_*`, `synthesis.*equivalence*`). Lesson of D16+D17: each new family lands under an ABSTRACT fmt\nword (`email`, `media`) with tool vocabulary (ffprobe). Next plausible (D18-D20): deeper `media.*` on a NON-WAV container\n(MP4/M4A voice memo atoms, AAC/MP3 codec params, WMA/ASF, AIFF/CAF), video/cover-art streams, images re-visited under an\nabstract `image.*` namespace (WebP/HEIC/TIFF, XMP DocumentID linking \"equivalent\" files), provenance (Zone.Identifier /\nquarantine xattr), and a synthesis key other than sha256 (size/time/duration order, codec grouping).\n\n## 1. Atlas\n\n| # | Concept / field | Status | Recognition cues | Standard tool / lib + exact call | D16+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Identity: filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | seen D1 (+D15 member roster) | any member; id stem names WHICH member | `hashlib.<algo>(b).hexdigest()`; `sha256sum` (I) | high -- every timed kit |\n| 2 | `file.magic_prefix_hex_N` | seen D2 | first N bytes | `xxd -p -l 16` (I); `b[:N].hex()` | high (carry-over) |\n| 3 | `text.utf8_bom_present` (utf16 sibling speculative) |