added to the STRUCT width (`_u16_hex` 4 digits, `_u32_hex` 8). GUIDs follow source.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nRanking (D17 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D18-D20 question with no extractor, or a harness blocker that silently fails a\nwhole family of prebuilds. TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail` for prebuild items.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"mp4-mov-atoms\", \"concept\": \"MP4/M4A/MOV/3GP atom metadata (voice memos, phone video)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (aliases audio, av, video, mp4, mov, quicktime). Box walk (size u32 BE, type; size 1 -> u64; size 0 -> to EOF). Fields: ftyp_major_brand (4 chars; emit rstrip'ed, plus ftyp_major_brand_raw verbatim), ftyp_minor_version, ftyp_compatible_brands (JSON, stored order), mvhd_creation_time_utc / mvhd_modification_time_utc (v0 u32 / v1 u64 seconds since 1904-01-01 -> ISO-8601 `Z`; ffprobe tag creation_time prints `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.000000Z`, emit that spelling under tag_creation_time), mvhd_timescale, mvhd_duration_seconds (duration/timescale, ffprobe-style 6 decimals), track_count, track_handler_types (JSON soun/vide/text), mdhd_languages (packed ISO-639-2 `und`), udta/ilst tags `©too` encoder, `©nam` title, `©day`, `©xyz` location (ISO 6709 string verbatim), mdta keys (`com.apple.quicktime.make/model/software/creationdate/location.ISO6709`) as tag_<key>. Pure struct; register via lib.meta like media_streams.py. Fixtures: build tiny m4a/mov with hand-packed boxes in the test (no ffmpeg needed).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-codec-params\", \"concept\": \"Codec-level parameters (AAC profile, MP3 frame/Xing/LAME, Opus/Vorbis details) in ffprobe vocabulary\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (+audio/av). Fields: primary_audio_profile (AAC AudioSpecificConfig object type from esds/ADTS: 2 -> `LC`, 5 -> `HE-AAC`, 29 -> `HE-AACv2`, 1 -> `Main`; ffprobe spelling), primary_audio_codec_long_name (ffprobe strings: `AAC (Advanced Audio Coding)`, `MP3 (MPEG audio layer 3)`, `PCM signed 16-bit little-endian`, `Opus (Opus Interactive Audio Codec)`, `Vorbis`, `FLAC (Free Lossless Audio Codec)`), mp3_mpeg_version, mp3_layer, mp3_bitrate_kbps (first frame), mp3_vbr_header (`Xing`/`Info`/`VBRI`/none), mp3_lame_encoder (9-char LAME tag e.g. `LAME3.100`), mp3_frame_count, primary_audio_sample_fmt for compressed codecs (aac/mp3 -> `fltp`, opus -> `fltp`, vorbis -> `fltp`, flac -> s16/s32 by bps). Verify spellings offline with the bundled ffmpeg -i.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"asf-aiff-caf-containers\", \"concept\": \"Other audio containers: ASF/WMA, AIFF/AIFC, CAF, AU, 3GP AMR\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (+audio/av; also fmt asf/aiff/caf aliases). Route by magic: ASF header GUID `30 26 b2 75 8e 66 cf 11 a6 d9 00 aa 00 62 ce 6c` -> Stream Properties audio WAVEFORMATEX tag (0x160 wmav1, 0x161 wmav2, 0x162 wmapro, 0x163 wmalossless, 0x0A wmavoice) + Content Description title/author/copyright/description + File Properties creation date (FILETIME) and play duration; AIFF `FORM....AIFF`/`AIFC` COMM: channels, numSampleFrames, sampleSize, 80-bit IEEE extended sample rate, AIFC compressionType (`NONE` -> pcm_s16be, `sowt` -> pcm_s16le, `fl32` -> pcm_f32be, `ulaw`/`alaw` -> pcm_mulaw/pcm_alaw, `ima4` -> adpcm_ima_qt) + NAME/AUTH/ANNO chunks; CAF `caff` desc chunk (float64 rate, formatID `lpcm`/`aac `/`alac`/`opus`/`ulaw`) + info chunk tags; Sun AU `.snd` encoding 1/2/3/27. Expose through primary_audio_codec_name/sample_rate/channels/container_format like the existing media modules (format_name ffprobe: `asf`, `aiff`, `caf`, `au`).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"synthesis-order-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Synthesis questions with a non-sha256 key (size/time/duration order, codec grouping)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis*.py (fmt synthesis) for ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>-order|groups|<x>` over the question's `Files: [...]` list (parse like digest_order; get_bytes per set): size_order (ascending bytes, ties -> filename), md5_order/sha1_order/sha512_order (generic algo from id), mtime_order (zip DOS mtime of each member from the container CD; also embedded timestamps: EXIF DateTimeOriginal, PDF CreationDate, email Date, mvhd creation), duration_order (media duration_seconds), codec_groups (JSON object codec_name -> sorted names), extension_mismatch_files (names whose magic != extension, file order), largest_file/smallest_file, newest_file/oldest_file. Descending only if the text says descending/newest first. Compact JSON.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"synthesis-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file md5/sha1/size ordering, duplicates, timeline\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) answered sha256 order D15-D17 (Files = note + 2 re-picked kit members + the day's new member; order re-rolls per Mastery set). D16 AND D17 timed modes both went solver_incomplete because the day's solver lacked the dispatch (D17 Mastery also needed the artifacts root set inside the per-set _solve_pairs worker). D17-night prebuild added equivalence/odd-one-out/thread groupings; non-hash ORDER keys are still open -> see synthesis-order-siblings.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"gate-allowlist-dfir-libs\", \"concept\": \"Prebuild gate refuses installed DFIR libs\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS lacks Evtx, regipy, olefile, oletools, dnfile, LnkParse3, lief, cryptography, asn1crypto, dpkt, PIL, sqlite3, wave, ordlookup. Targets evtx-records (python-evtx) and regf-values (regipy) as written will fail the gate exactly like pe-debug-rich-imports did (import ordlookup). Either widen the allowlist (all are in .venv) or rewrite those goals as stdlib/struct parsers. Also `open` is banned: regipy RegistryHive needs a path -> use a struct nk/vk walker.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xmp-packets\", \"concept\": \"XMP packet fields in any container (DocumentID lineage)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt xmp (also registered under jpeg/png/pdf/media/ooxml/image as xmp_<field>). Find `<x:xmpmeta` ... `</x:xmpmeta>` (or `<?xpacket begin` ... `<?xpacket end`) anywhere in the bytes (JPEG APP1 `http://ns.adobe.com/xap/1.0/\\\\0`, PNG iTXt `XML:com.adobe.xmp`, PDF Metadata stream if uncompressed, MP4 `uuid` BE7ACFCB-97A9-42E8-9C71-999491E3AFAC, WAV `_PMX` chunk). Parse with xml.etree (namespaces by URI, rdf:Description attributes AND child elements, rdf:Seq/Alt/Bag -> lists). Fields: document_id, instance_id, original_document_id (verbatim incl. `xmp.did:`/`uuid:` prefixes), derived_from_document_id, history_actions (JSON, stored order), history_software_agents, creator_tool, create_date, modify_date, metadata_date (verbatim), dc_creator (JSON list), dc_title (x-default), dc_format. Synthesis helper: files sharing document_id/original_document_id.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"image-modern-containers\", \"concept\": \"WebP / TIFF / HEIC-AVIF / ICC under an abstract `image.*` fmt\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt image (alias also for existing jpeg/png/gif/bmp fields: image.dimensions_pixels routes by magic to SOF/IHDR/LSD/DIB) + webp, tiff, heic. WebP `RIFF....WEBP`: VP8 (frame tag, 14-bit w/h after `9d 01 2a`), VP8L (`2f` + 14-bit w-1/h-1), VP8X (canvas 24-bit w-1/h-1, flags ICC/alpha/EXIF/XMP/anim), chunk_ids JSON, has_exif/has_xmp/has_icc, animation frame_count. TIFF `II*\\\\0`/`MM\\\\0*`: byte_order, ifd0 ImageWidth/ImageLength/Make/Model/Software/DateTime/Artist, ifd_count. HEIC/AVIF `ftyp heic|heix|mif1|avif`: major_brand, ispe width x height of the primary item (pitm), item count, Exif item presence. ICC (APP2 ICC_PROFILE / PNG iCCP zlib / WebP ICCP): profile_description (desc/mluc), color_space, device_class, version. Answer formats like D4/D5: `<w>x<h>`.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"subtitle-chapter-streams\", \"concept\": \"Cover art, subtitle and chapter streams (ffprobe stream accounting)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (+av/video). ffprobe counts an embedded cover (ID3 APIC, MP4 `covr`, FLAC PICTURE block, MKV attachment with image mime) as a VIDEO stream with codec_name `mjpeg`/`png` and disposition attached_pic=1 -> fields attached_pic_present, attached_pic_codec_name, attached_pic_mime_type, attached_pic_dimensions_pixels, nb_streams_including_cover (document the difference vs audio_stream_count). Subtitles: MP4 `tx3g` -> `mov_text`, MKV S_TEXT/UTF8 -> `subrip`, S_TEXT/ASS -> `ass`, S_TEXT/WEBVTT -> `webvtt`; fields subtitle_stream_count, subtitle_codec_names (stream order), subtitle_languages. Chapters: MP4 `chpl`/QuickTime chapter track, MKV EditionEntry/ChapterAtom -> chapter_count, chapter_titles (JSON), chapter_start_times_seconds.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"zone-identifier-motw\", \"concept\": \"Download provenance: Zone.Identifier ADS, macOS quarantine, AppleDouble\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt zone_identifier (aliases motw, ads): text `[ZoneTransfer]` INI (UTF-8/UTF-16 with BOM): zone_id (int), zone_name (0 Local,1 Intranet,2 Trusted,3 Internet,4 Restricted), referrer_url, host_url, last_writer_package_family_name, app_zone_id -- values verbatim. Member names like `x.exe:Zone.Identifier` or `x.exe_Zone.Identifier`. fmt quarantine: `com.apple.quarantine` value `flags;hex_unix_time;agent;uuid` -> quarantine_flags_hex, quarantine_time_utc, quarantine_agent, quarantine_event_uuid. fmt appledouble: `00 05 16 07` header, entry table (id 2 resource fork, 9 Finder info with `ATTR` xattr block) -> xattr_names (JSON), xattr_<name> (UTF-8 if printable else hex), finder_type_creator.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"archives-tar-7z-iso\", \"concept\": \"TAR / 7z / RAR / ISO9660-UDF headers (archives gap only produced gzip)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt archives were not registered by the earlier `archives` run (tar/7z/rar/iso have 0 fields). Separate modules: tar (ustar_magic, member_names stored order, member_sizes, member_mtimes_utc, member_modes_octal, member_unames/gnames, typeflags) via tarfile.open(fileobj=io.BytesIO(b)); 7z (signature_version `0.4`, next_header_offset/size, start_header_crc32_hex, has_encrypted_header when the next header is kEncodedHeader with AES coder 06f10701); rar (version 4|5, RAR5 main archive flags, file names when headers unencrypted, is_header_encrypted); iso (pvd system_id, volume_id, volume_set_id, publisher_id, application_id (strip spaces), volume_creation_date_utc from 17-byte dec-datetime @813 with GMT offset, volume_space_size, logical_block_size, joliet_present (SVD escape %/@ %/C %/E), udf_present (BEA01/NSR02/NSR03), root_member_names). fmt `archive` alias for all.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-fmt-alias\", \"concept\": \"GM fmt `media` -> prebuilt `wav`/`mp3` fields + D17 codec name in lib\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/media.py registering fmt 'media' (aliases 'audio', 'av') that routes by MAGIC to the existing wav/mp3/gif... extractors, and registers ('media','primary_audio_codec_name') (GM-verified D17: 16-bit PCM WAV -> 'pcm_s16le') by porting challenges/day17/metadata-hear-me-out/solver/solve.py _audio_codec (RIFF/RIFX/RF64, AIFF/AIFC, fLaC, Ogg Opus/Vorbis/FLAC/Speex, AMR, .snd, MP4 stsd, Matroska CodecID, MPEG/ADTS sync). Do NOT change the pcm_s16le mapping. D16 lesson repeated: an extractor under the container's fmt word is invisible to the GM's namespace.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-stream-fields\", \"concept\": \"ffprobe-style stream/format fields for the first audio stream\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields primary_audio_sample_rate_hz (also _sample_rate), primary_audio_channels, primary_audio_channel_layout (ffprobe: mono/stereo/2.1/quad/5.1...), primary_audio_bits_per_sample (ffprobe bits_per_sample; 0 for lossy), primary_audio_sample_fmt (u8/s16/s32/flt/dbl; planar 'fltp' for aac/opus/vorbis decoders), primary_audio_bit_rate (bps integer: PCM = rate*ch*bits), primary_audio_codec_long_name ('PCM signed 16-bit little-endian'), primary_audio_codec_tag_hex ('0x0001'), primary_audio_codec_tag_string ffprobe-style, primary_audio_duration_seconds (string with 6 decimals like ffprobe '1.250000'), primary_audio_nb_samples / duration_ts, format_name (ffprobe demuxer: wav, mp3, ogg, flac, aiff, amr, au, 'mov,mp4,m4a,3gp,3g2,mj2', 'matroska,webm'), format_long_name, nb_streams, audio_stream_count, format_duration_seconds, format_size_bytes, format_bit_rate. WAV: data chunk size / byte rate; MP3: Xing/Info/VBRI frames or frame walk; Ogg: last page granule / rate (Opus 48 kHz minus pre_skip); FLAC: STREAMINFO total samples; MP4: mdhd timescale/duration.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-wav-deep\", \"concept\": \"WAV chunk-level metadata (BWF bext, fact, LIST/INFO, cue, iXML, data-vs-RIFF size, trailing bytes)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media + wav alias, fields riff_chunk_ids (file order JSON), info_title (INAM; D17 carried 'Huntress audio evidence <12 hex>'), info_software (ISFT), info_creation_date (ICRD), info_comment (ICMT), info_artist (IART), bext_description, bext_originator, bext_originator_reference, bext_origination_date, bext_origination_time, bext_time_reference, bext_umid_hex, fact_sample_count, data_chunk_size_bytes, riff_size_declared, riff_size_mismatch (declared+8 != len), trailing_bytes_after_data (count + magic_prefix_hex_16 of the trailer -> hidden payload), cue_point_count, ixml_present. Pure struct; values verbatim (strip trailing NULs).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-renamed-containers\", \"concept\": \"Renamed/transcoded audio: actual container + codec vs the extension\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields container_format (by magic: wav/rf64/aiff/mp3/ogg/flac/mp4/matroska/amr/au/adts/caf/wma-asf), declared_extension, extension_matches_content (true/false), mime_type_by_magic (audio/wav, audio/mpeg, audio/ogg, audio/flac, audio/mp4, audio/amr), plus primary_audio_codec_name for: ASF/WMA (GUID 3026b275 + stream props -> wmav2), CAF ('caff' desc fourcc), MP4 esds objectTypeIndication (0x40 aac, 0x6b mp3), Ogg multiple codecs. Flavor D17: 'Voice notes have been transcoded, renamed'.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-multistream\", \"concept\": \"Per-stream fields in multi-stream containers; the odd stream\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields stream_codec_names (JSON, container stream index order like ffprobe), audio_stream_codec_names, stream_languages (MP4 mdhd packed ISO-639-2 / MKV Language default 'eng' / 'und'), stream_titles (MKV Name, MP4 udta name/handler_name), stream_creation_times_utc (mdhd 1904 epoch), stream_durations_seconds, stream_sample_rates, primary_video_codec_name, odd_stream_index (the one whose codec/language/rate/creation_time differs from the majority -- emit index and a JSON diagnostic). MP4 box walk moov/trak/mdia/{mdhd,hdlr,minf/stbl/stsd}; Matroska EBML walk Segment/Tracks/TrackEntry (TrackType 2=audio, CodecID map A_OPUS opus, A_VORBIS vorbis, A_AAC aac, A_FLAC flac, A_MPEG/L3 mp3, A_PCM/INT/LIT pcm_s16le by BitDepth, A_AC3 ac3, V_MPEG4/ISO/AVC h264, V_MPEGH/ISO/HEVC hevc, V_VP9 vp9, V_AV1 av1); Ogg: group pages by serial, BOS packet per stream. Flavor D17: 'find the stream that breaks the sender's story'.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-format-tags\", \"concept\": \"Container/stream tags: title, artist, comment, encoder, creation_time, language\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields tag_title, tag_artist, tag_album, tag_comment, tag_encoder, tag_date, tag_creation_time_utc, tag_<key> generic (lowercase ffprobe key), encoder (ffprobe format tag 'encoder': ID3 TSSE, Vorbis/Opus ENCODER + vendor string, MP4 \\\\xa9too, MKV MuxingApp/WritingApp, WAV ISFT), opus_vendor / vorbis_vendor, id3_version. Sources: WAV LIST/INFO, ID3v2.2-2.4 (+v1), Vorbis comment (Ogg/FLAC/Opus OpusTags), MP4 moov/udta/meta/ilst, MKV Tags. Reuse prebuilt mp3/wav parsers where possible; stdlib only (mutagen is not allowlisted).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"email-media-attachments\", \"concept\": \"Audio embedded in mail: MIME audio attachments + member resolution through .eml\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email (+eml/mime aliases), fields attachment_audio_codec_names (MIME order, via the media codec extractor on decoded payloads), attachment_media_container_formats, attachment_declared_content_types, attachment_audio_mismatch_names (declared Content-Type/extension vs actual codec), attachment_audio_durations_seconds, audio_attachment_count. Also expose lib.meta.prebuilt helper attachment_bytes(eml_bytes, filename) (RFC 2231/2047 filename decode, get_payload(decode=True)) so artifact refs like `message-001.eml -> voice-001.ogg` and `zip -> eml -> wav` resolve. Flavor D17: 'embedded in mail'.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"media-equivalence-synthesis\", \"concept\": \"Cross-recording equivalence / odd-one-out synthesis\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Add to lib.meta.synthesis: equivalence_groups(question, get_bytes) over the `Files: [...]` audio members -> group by (1) shared title/correlation tag (WAV INAM, ID3 TIT2, Vorbis TITLE, MP4 \\\\xa9nam; D17 INAM 'Huntress audio evidence <12 hex>'), (2) equal decoded duration rounded to 10 ms / equal sample count, (3) equal PCM data-chunk sha256 or FLAC STREAMINFO MD5; outputs compact JSON array of arrays of filenames (each group sorted, groups by first name), the odd_one_out filename, duplicate_count. Also md5/sha1/size-order variants of digest_order (synthesis-siblings). Spelling unverified -> keep alternates.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tool-ffprobe\", \"concept\": \"ffprobe/ffmpeg + sox for media ground truth\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"PARTLY SOLVED: ffmpeg 7.0.2 ships at tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2 (imageio-ffmpeg; not on PATH, no ffprobe). `ffmpeg -hide_banner -i f` prints ffprobe vocabulary (`Stream #0:0: Audio: pcm_s16le ([1][0][0][0] / 0x0001), 16000 Hz, mono, s16`, format tags) -- verified on D17. Still wanted: a bin/ shim `ffmpeg` on PATH and a real ffprobe (static build) for `-show_streams -show_format -of json`; apt sox (soxi). Worker/offline verification only, never in-window.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"email-fmt-alias\", \"concept\": \"GM fmt `email` -> prebuilt `eml` fields\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"New module lib/meta/prebuilt/email.py re-registering EVERY ('eml', f) field of lib/meta/prebuilt/eml.py under fmt 'email' (also 'mail', 'mime') with the same extractor. D16 GM asked email.message_id; the eml-registered extractor was invisible to the solver. Message-ID verbatim WITH angle brackets (GM-verified D16).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"email-threading\", \"concept\": \"In-Reply-To / References / thread root / reply-forward flags\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email (+eml alias), fields in_reply_to, references (compact JSON list, stored order, each id with <>), references_count, thread_root_message_id (References[0] else In-Reply-To else own Message-ID), parent_message_id (last References id else In-Reply-To), is_reply, is_forward (Re:/Fwd:/FW: prefix or X-Forwarded-*), normalized_subject (strip Re:/Fwd: repeatedly), thread_index_guid (Outlook Thread-Index base64: 22-byte header = FILETIME-ish 6 B + GUID 16 B), thread_topic, resent_message_id, header_<name> generic (first occurrence, unfolded, verbatim). stdlib email only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"email-mime-attachments\", \"concept\": \"MIME tree, attachment names/sizes/hashes/types\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt email, fields mime_part_count, content_type (top-level, no params), mime_boundary, attachment_count, attachment_names (MIME order), attachment_content_types, attachment_sizes_bytes (decoded), attachment_sha256s / md5s / sha1s (decoded payload), attachment_magic_prefix_hex_16, attachment_declared_vs_magic_mismatch, body_text_sha256, content_transfer_encodings. msg.walk() + get_payload(decode=True); RFC 2231/2047 filenames decoded.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mbox-collection\", \"concept\": \"MBOX / mailbox export: count, ids, duplicates, threads\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt mbox (alias mailbox), fields message_count, message_ids (file order, with <>), unique_message_id_count, duplicate_message_ids (sorted), thread_count, thread_root_ids, subjects, first_date_utc, last_date_utc. Split bytes on b'\\\\nFrom ' (first line at 0), unescape '>From ', parse each with email.message_from_bytes (stdlib mailbox needs a path -> not allowed).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"email-thread-synthesis\", \"concept\": \"Cross-message threading over several .eml members\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D16 flavor: 'rebuild which mail actually belongs together'. Add to lib.meta.synthesis: thread_groups(question, get_bytes) over the `Files: [...]` list -> group by thread root (References/In-Reply-To, union-find), dedupe by Message-ID, order members by Date then filename; outputs: compact JSON array of arrays (filenames), thread_count, duplicate filenames, root filename per thread. Spelling unverified -> register sorted-filename variant and keep date order as an alternate.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pe-debug-rich-imports\", \"concept\": \"PE PDB path / Rich header / imphash / imports / exports / Authenticode\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Re-run the REJECTED target without `import ordlookup` (pefile.PE.get_imphash already handles ordinals). fmt pe, fields debug_pdb_path, debug_codeview_guid, debug_codeview_age, rich_header_hash_md5, rich_header_xor_key_u32_hex, imphash, import_dll_names, export_names, export_dll_name. Do not re-register time_date_stamp_u32_hex (exists).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pe-authenticode\", \"concept\": \"PE Authenticode signer / cert serial / thumbprint / signing time\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt pe, fields is_signed, security_dir_size_u32_hex, signer_subject_cn, signer_issuer_cn, signer_serial_hex, signer_cert_sha1, signer_cert_sha256, signing_time_utc. Data dir 4 VirtualAddress is a file offset; WIN_CERTIFICATE (len u32, rev 0x0200, type 2) + PKCS#7 SignedData. Needs asn1crypto/cryptography in ALLOWED_IMPORTS or a minimal stdlib DER walker.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"evtx-records\", \"concept\": \"EVTX record fields (EventID, TimeCreated, Provider, Channel, Computer, count)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt evtx: record_count, first_event_id, first_time_created_utc, provider_names, channel, computer_name) + event_ids (ordered list), last_event_record_id, event_data_<name> family. Blocked by gate-allowlist-dfir-libs unless a stdlib BinXML walker is written (template substitution makes that ~400 lines; widening the allowlist for Evtx is cheaper).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"regf-values\", \"concept\": \"Registry key/value lookups (Run keys, last-write, counts, UserAssist)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt regf: run_key_values, last_written_utc, subkey_count, value_count, userassist_entries) + value_<path> family, computer_name, timezone_key_name. Use a struct nk/vk/lf/lh/ri walker over hbins (stdlib) since regipy needs a file path and is not allowlisted.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"recycle-bin-i\", \"concept\": \"Recycle Bin $I original path / deletion time / size\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Split from target jumplist-recycle-mft so it lands alone: fmt recycle (also alias fmt recyclebin), fields original_path, deleted_time_utc, original_size, format_version. v1: header=1, size u64@8, FILETIME@16, UTF-16 path 520 B@24; v2: header=2, path chars u32@24, path@28. Pure struct, ~40 lines.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"prefetch\", \"concept\": \"Prefetch exe name / run count / last run times / volume info\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Existing TARGET (fmt prefetch: executable_name, run_count, last_run_time_utc, format_version, prefetch_hash_u32_hex, volume_serial_u32_hex) + last_run_times_utc (list of 8), volume_device_path, referenced_file_count. Uncompressed SCCA v17/23/26/30 is struct-only; Win10 MAM\\\\x04 needs an LZXpress-Huffman decoder (stdlib port ~120 lines, or tool dissect.util).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"task-xml\", \"concept\": \"Scheduled task XML (Command, Arguments, Author, Date, URI, Triggers)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt task (aliases scheduled_task, task_xml), fields exec_command, exec_arguments, registration_author, registration_date, uri, principal_user_id, run_level, trigger_types, hidden. UTF-16LE BOM XML, ns http://schemas.microsoft.com/windows/2004/02/mit/task; xml.etree with local-name matching.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ole-vba\", \"concept\": \"VBA macro project (module names, auto-exec, stomping)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt vba (and ole alias fields), fields module_names, project_name, has_macros, autoexec_keywords, vba_stream_names, code_page. Reuse lib/meta/cfb.py cfb_streams; dir stream is MS-OVBA RLE-compressed (port the ~40-line decompress","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/12ea224e-c03c-442e-a972-e0c7035f8c2a/tool-results/b8io6kcpg.txt","persistedOutputSize":41542},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PDDgaMEcFywekNyPMedWwB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
