{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VqNz6k3HbSvJQRRL3tt6mH","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"id\": \"mp4-mov-atoms\", \"concept\": \"MP4/M4A/MOV/3GP atom metadata (voice memos, phone video)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (aliases audio, av, video, mp4, mov, quicktime). Box walk (size u32 BE, type; size 1 -> u64; size 0 -> to EOF). Fields: ftyp_major_brand (4 chars; emit rstrip'ed, plus ftyp_major_brand_raw verbatim), ftyp_minor_version, ftyp_compatible_brands (JSON, stored order), mvhd_creation_time_utc / mvhd_modification_time_utc (v0 u32 / v1 u64 seconds since 1904-01-01 -> ISO-8601 `Z`; ffprobe tag creation_time prints `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.000000Z`, emit that spelling under tag_creation_time), mvhd_timescale, mvhd_duration_seconds (duration/timescale, ffprobe-style 6 decimals), track_count, track_handler_types (JSON soun/vide/text), mdhd_languages (packed ISO-639-2 `und`), udta/ilst tags `\\u00a9too` encoder, `\\u00a9nam` title, `\\u00a9day`, `\\u00a9xyz` location (ISO 6709 string verbatim), mdta keys (`com.apple.quicktime.make/model/software/creationdate/location.ISO6709`) as tag_<key>. Pure struct; register via lib.meta like media_streams.py. Fixtures: build tiny m4a/mov with hand-packed boxes in the test (no ffmpeg needed).\"} \n\n{\"id\": \"synthesis-order-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Synthesis questions with a non-sha256 key (size/time/duration order, codec grouping)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis*.py (fmt synthesis) for ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>-order|groups|<x>` over the question's `Files: [...]` list (parse like digest_order; get_bytes per set): size_order (ascending bytes, ties -> filename), md5_order/sha1_order/sha512_order (generic algo from id), mtime_order (zip DOS mtime of each member from the container CD; also embedded timestamps: EXIF DateTimeOriginal, PDF CreationDate, email Date, mvhd creation), duration_order (media duration_seconds), codec_groups (JSON object codec_name -> sorted names), extension_mismatch_files (names whose magic != extension, file order), largest_file/smallest_file, newest_file/oldest_file. Descending only if the text says descending/newest first. Compact JSON.\"} \n\n{\"id\": \"synthesis-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file md5/sha1/size ordering, duplicates, timeline\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) answered sha256 order D15-D17 (Files = note + 2 re-picked kit members + the day's new member; order re-rolls per Mastery set). D16 AND D17 timed modes both went solver_incomplete because the day's solver lacked the dispatch (D17 Mastery also needed the artifacts root set inside the per-set _solve_pairs worker). D17-night prebuild added equivalence/odd-one-out/thread groupings; non-hash ORDER keys are still open -> see synthesis-order-siblings.\"} \n\n{\"id\": \"image-modern-containers\", \"concept\": \"WebP / TIFF / HEIC-AVIF / ICC under an abstract `image.*` fmt\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt image (alias also for existing jpeg/png/gif/bmp fields: image.dimensions_pixels routes by magic to SOF/IHDR/LSD/DIB) + webp, tiff, heic. WebP `RIFF....WEBP`: VP8 (frame tag, 14-bit w/h after `9d 01 2a`), VP8L (`2f` + 14-bit w-1/h-1), VP8X (canvas 24-bit w-1/h-1, flags ICC/alpha/EXIF/XMP/anim), chunk_ids JSON, has_exif/has_xmp/has_icc, animation frame_count. TIFF `II*\\\\0`/`MM\\\\0*`: byte_order, ifd0 ImageWidth/ImageLength/Make/Model/Software/DateTime/Artist, ifd_count. HEIC/AVIF `ftyp heic|heix|mif1|avif`: major_brand, ispe width x height of the primary item (pitm), item count, Exif item presence. ICC (APP2 ICC_PROFILE / PNG iCCP zlib / WebP ICCP): profile_description (desc/mluc), color_space, device_class, version. Answer formats like D4/D5: `<w>x<h>`.\"} \n\n{\"id\": \"subtitle-chapter-streams\", \"concept\": \"Cover art, subtitle and chapter streams (ffprobe stream accounting)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (+av/video). ffprobe counts an embedded cover (ID3 APIC, MP4 `covr`, FLAC PICTURE block, MKV attachment with image mime) as a VIDEO stream with codec_name `mjpeg`/`png` and disposition attached_pic=1 -> fields attached_pic_present, attached_pic_codec_name, attached_pic_mime_type, attached_pic_dimensions_pixels, nb_streams_including_cover (document the difference vs audio_stream_count). Subtitles: MP4 `tx3g` -> `mov_text`, MKV S_TEXT/UTF8 -> `subrip`, S_TEXT/ASS -> `ass`, S_TEXT/WEBVTT -> `webvtt`; fields subtitle_stream_count, subtitle_codec_names (stream order), subtitle_languages. Chapters: MP4 `chpl`/QuickTime chapter track, MKV EditionEntry/ChapterAtom -> chapter_count, chapter_titles (JSON), chapter_start_times_seconds.\"} \n\n{\"id\": \"tool-ffprobe\", \"concept\": \"ffprobe/ffmpeg + sox for media ground truth\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"PARTLY SOLVED: ffmpeg 7.0.2 ships at tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2 (imageio-ffmpeg; not on PATH, no ffprobe). `ffmpeg -hide_banner -i f` prints ffprobe vocabulary (`Stream #0:0: Audio: pcm_s16le ([1][0][0][0] / 0x0001), 16000 Hz, mono, s16`, format tags) -- verified on D17. Still wanted: a bin/ shim `ffmpeg` on PATH and a real ffprobe (static build) for `-show_streams -show_format -of json`; apt sox (soxi). Worker/offline verification only, never in-window.\"} \n\n{\"id\": \"media-video-streams\", \"concept\": \"Video stream fields (codec, dimensions, frame rate, pix_fmt, rotation)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields primary_video_codec_name (h264, hevc, vp8, vp9, av1, mpeg4, mjpeg, prores), primary_video_width, primary_video_height, primary_video_dimensions_pixels ('<w>x<h>' like D4/D5), primary_video_frame_rate ('30000/1001' r_frame_rate), primary_video_pix_fmt (avcC/hvcC chroma -> yuv420p), primary_video_profile, rotation (tkhd matrix / displaymatrix), video_stream_count. MP4 stsd avc1/hvc1/hev1/vp09/av01/mp4v, MKV CodecID, AVI RIFF 'AVI ' strh/strf fourcc (H264, XVID, MJPG).\"} \n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nRanking (D17 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D18-D20 question with no extractor, or a harness blocker that silently fails a\nwhole family of prebuilds. TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail` for prebuild items.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"12ea224e-c03c-442e-a972-e0c7035f8c2a","uuid":"57317d79-bc58-4909-aa69-edcb2ec5cabe","timestamp":"2026-10-18T13:03:32.734Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\"id\": \"mp4-mov-atoms\", \"concept\": \"MP4/M4A/MOV/3GP atom metadata (voice memos, phone video)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (aliases audio, av, video, mp4, mov, quicktime). Box walk (size u32 BE, type; size 1 -> u64; size 0 -> to EOF). Fields: ftyp_major_brand (4 chars; emit rstrip'ed, plus ftyp_major_brand_raw verbatim), ftyp_minor_version, ftyp_compatible_brands (JSON, stored order), mvhd_creation_time_utc / mvhd_modification_time_utc (v0 u32 / v1 u64 seconds since 1904-01-01 -> ISO-8601 `Z`; ffprobe tag creation_time prints `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.000000Z`, emit that spelling under tag_creation_time), mvhd_timescale, mvhd_duration_seconds (duration/timescale, ffprobe-style 6 decimals), track_count, track_handler_types (JSON soun/vide/text), mdhd_languages (packed ISO-639-2 `und`), udta/ilst tags `\\u00a9too` encoder, `\\u00a9nam` title, `\\u00a9day`, `\\u00a9xyz` location (ISO 6709 string verbatim), mdta keys (`com.apple.quicktime.make/model/software/creationdate/location.ISO6709`) as tag_<key>. Pure struct; register via lib.meta like media_streams.py. Fixtures: build tiny m4a/mov with hand-packed boxes in the test (no ffmpeg needed).\"} \n\n{\"id\": \"synthesis-order-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Synthesis questions with a non-sha256 key (size/time/duration order, codec grouping)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend lib/meta/prebuilt/synthesis*.py (fmt synthesis) for ids `metadata-day-NN-synthesis-<key>-order|groups|<x>` over the question's `Files: [...]` list (parse like digest_order; get_bytes per set): size_order (ascending bytes, ties -> filename), md5_order/sha1_order/sha512_order (generic algo from id), mtime_order (zip DOS mtime of each member from the container CD; also embedded timestamps: EXIF DateTimeOriginal, PDF CreationDate, email Date, mvhd creation), duration_order (media duration_seconds), codec_groups (JSON object codec_name -> sorted names), extension_mismatch_files (names whose magic != extension, file order), largest_file/smallest_file, newest_file/oldest_file. Descending only if the text says descending/newest first. Compact JSON.\"} \n\n{\"id\": \"synthesis-siblings\", \"concept\": \"Cross-file md5/sha1/size ordering, duplicates, timeline\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"lib.meta.synthesis.digest_order(question, get_bytes, algo) answered sha256 order D15-D17 (Files = note + 2 re-picked kit members + the day's new member; order re-rolls per Mastery set). D16 AND D17 timed modes both went solver_incomplete because the day's solver lacked the dispatch (D17 Mastery also needed the artifacts root set inside the per-set _solve_pairs worker). D17-night prebuild added equivalence/odd-one-out/thread groupings; non-hash ORDER keys are still open -> see synthesis-order-siblings.\"} \n\n{\"id\": \"image-modern-containers\", \"concept\": \"WebP / TIFF / HEIC-AVIF / ICC under an abstract `image.*` fmt\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt image (alias also for existing jpeg/png/gif/bmp fields: image.dimensions_pixels routes by magic to SOF/IHDR/LSD/DIB) + webp, tiff, heic. WebP `RIFF....WEBP`: VP8 (frame tag, 14-bit w/h after `9d 01 2a`), VP8L (`2f` + 14-bit w-1/h-1), VP8X (canvas 24-bit w-1/h-1, flags ICC/alpha/EXIF/XMP/anim), chunk_ids JSON, has_exif/has_xmp/has_icc, animation frame_count. TIFF `II*\\\\0`/`MM\\\\0*`: byte_order, ifd0 ImageWidth/ImageLength/Make/Model/Software/DateTime/Artist, ifd_count. HEIC/AVIF `ftyp heic|heix|mif1|avif`: major_brand, ispe width x height of the primary item (pitm), item count, Exif item presence. ICC (APP2 ICC_PROFILE / PNG iCCP zlib / WebP ICCP): profile_description (desc/mluc), color_space, device_class, version. Answer formats like D4/D5: `<w>x<h>`.\"} \n\n{\"id\": \"subtitle-chapter-streams\", \"concept\": \"Cover art, subtitle and chapter streams (ffprobe stream accounting)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media (+av/video). ffprobe counts an embedded cover (ID3 APIC, MP4 `covr`, FLAC PICTURE block, MKV attachment with image mime) as a VIDEO stream with codec_name `mjpeg`/`png` and disposition attached_pic=1 -> fields attached_pic_present, attached_pic_codec_name, attached_pic_mime_type, attached_pic_dimensions_pixels, nb_streams_including_cover (document the difference vs audio_stream_count). Subtitles: MP4 `tx3g` -> `mov_text`, MKV S_TEXT/UTF8 -> `subrip`, S_TEXT/ASS -> `ass`, S_TEXT/WEBVTT -> `webvtt`; fields subtitle_stream_count, subtitle_codec_names (stream order), subtitle_languages. Chapters: MP4 `chpl`/QuickTime chapter track, MKV EditionEntry/ChapterAtom -> chapter_count, chapter_titles (JSON), chapter_start_times_seconds.\"} \n\n{\"id\": \"tool-ffprobe\", \"concept\": \"ffprobe/ffmpeg + sox for media ground truth\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"PARTLY SOLVED: ffmpeg 7.0.2 ships at tools/imageio_ffmpeg_pkg/imageio_ffmpeg/binaries/ffmpeg-linux-x86_64-v7.0.2 (imageio-ffmpeg; not on PATH, no ffprobe). `ffmpeg -hide_banner -i f` prints ffprobe vocabulary (`Stream #0:0: Audio: pcm_s16le ([1][0][0][0] / 0x0001), 16000 Hz, mono, s16`, format tags) -- verified on D17. Still wanted: a bin/ shim `ffmpeg` on PATH and a real ffprobe (static build) for `-show_streams -show_format -of json`; apt sox (soxi). Worker/offline verification only, never in-window.\"} \n\n{\"id\": \"media-video-streams\", \"concept\": \"Video stream fields (codec, dimensions, frame rate, pix_fmt, rotation)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"fmt media, fields primary_video_codec_name (h264, hevc, vp8, vp9, av1, mpeg4, mjpeg, prores), primary_video_width, primary_video_height, primary_video_dimensions_pixels ('<w>x<h>' like D4/D5), primary_video_frame_rate ('30000/1001' r_frame_rate), primary_video_pix_fmt (avcC/hvcC chroma -> yuv420p), primary_video_profile, rotation (tkhd matrix / displaymatrix), video_stream_count. MP4 stsd avc1/hvc1/hev1/vp09/av01/mp4v, MKV CodecID, AVI RIFF 'AVI ' strh/strf fourcc (H264, XVID, MJPG).\"} \n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nRanking (D17 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D18-D20 question with no extractor, or a harness blocker that silently fails a\nwhole family of prebuilds. TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail` for prebuild items.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VqNz6k3HbSvJQRRL3tt6mH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
