{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9keNZxFGLMkE7CQhRnM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Dx5bNhLcinS3SJnotd6axq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'E'\nimport json\np='reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md'; s=open(p).read()\npre,rest=s.split('## Readiness gaps',1)\nintro,body=rest.split('```json',1)\njs,after=body.split('```',1)\nG=json.loads(js)\nids=[g['id'] for g in G]\nG=[g for g in G if g['id']!='media-video-streams']\nby={g['id']:g for g in G}\nby['asf-aiff-caf-containers']['priority']=2\nby['image-modern-containers']['priority']=1\nby['image-modern-containers']['detail']+=\" D18 flavor 'previews' + one-namespace-per-family drift: build together with media-image-as-video-stream (same dims parsers, fmt image AND media).\"\nby['mp4-mov-atoms']['detail']+=\" D18 video-001.mp4 (Lavf: ftyp isom/512/isomiso2avc1mp41, udta/meta hdlr mdta keys=[title] -> `Huntress MP4 evidence <12 HEX>`, handler_name VideoHandler/SoundHandler, encoder `Lavc libx264`) is a ready fixture shape; device keys feed video-device-provenance.\"\nby['synthesis-siblings']['detail']+=\" D18: Files = note + panel-001.png + installer-001.msi + video-001.mp4; the single worker pre-wired the dispatch -> TT 23 / Mastery 115 CORRECT in-window first try.\"\nby['tool-ffprobe']['detail']+=\" D18: the same `ffmpeg -i` line verified video geometry (`h264 (High) (avc1 / 0x31637661), yuv420p(progressive), 320x180 [SAR 1:1 DAR 16:9], 10 fps`).\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"media-image-as-video-stream\",\"concept\":\"Still images asked through `media.*` (ffprobe opens JPEG/PNG/GIF/BMP/WebP as one video stream)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"BUG-LEVEL GAP: on the D18 TT kit, lib.meta.answer('d18-video-001-media-primary-video-dimensions', data=camera-001.jpg / panel-001.png) returns ('none','verified') and audio-001.wav returns (None, None). ffprobe reports a still as stream 0 codec_type video: JPEG -> codec_name mjpeg (demuxer jpeg_pipe/image2, pix_fmt yuvj420p/yuvj422p/yuvj444p/gray from SOF sampling), PNG -> png (rgb24/rgba/gray/ya8/pal8/rgb48be/rgba64be from IHDR bit depth+colour type), GIF -> gif (bgra), BMP -> bmp (bgr24/bgra/pal8), WebP -> webp, TIFF -> tiff. Fix in lib/meta/prebuilt (new module media_stills.py registering fmt media/video/av, or extend media_video): primary_video_dimensions(_pixels)/width/height from SOF/IHDR/LSD/DIB/VP8 headers (`<w>x<h>`, same as D4/D5), primary_video_codec_name, primary_video_pix_fmt, nb_streams 1, primary_audio_* -> `none`; an audio-only WAV/MP3 -> literal `none` for every primary_video_* field (absent stream), not None. Fixtures: the kit's jpg/png from any day18 solver case + the bundled ffmpeg -i to confirm the expected spellings offline.\"},\n {\"id\":\"video-geometry-crop-aspect\",\"concept\":\"Crop / aspect / display geometry of the primary video stream\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D18 flavor 'originals, crops'. fmt media (+video/av). ffprobe semantics: width/height = decoder output = SPS size after frame_cropping (h264: (pic_width_in_mbs*16 - CropUnitX*(left+right)); hevc conf_win_*), coded_width/coded_height = MB/CTB-aligned size; sample_aspect_ratio `N:M` from pasp (else SPS VUI aspect_ratio_idc table, else `1:1`/`0:1` when unknown), display_aspect_ratio = reduced (w*sarN):(h*sarD) e.g. `16:9`. Fields: primary_video_sample_aspect_ratio, primary_video_display_aspect_ratio, primary_video_coded_width/height/dimensions, sps_dimensions_pixels, stsd_dimensions_pixels, tkhd_dimensions_pixels (16.16 -> int when whole, else 3 decimals), display_dimensions_pixels (tkhd size; swapped when |rotation| = 90), clean_aperture_dimensions (clap widthN/D, heightN/D, horizOff, vertOff), tapt_clef/prof/enof dimensions (QuickTime), mkv_pixel_crop (Top/Bottom/Left/Right) + DisplayWidth/DisplayHeight/DisplayUnit, is_cropped (true when SPS crop/clap/PixelCrop non-zero or tkhd < coded), geometry_mismatch (stsd vs SPS vs tkhd disagree). ALSO: make primary_video_dimensions prefer the SPS-cropped size when an SPS is present (ffprobe), stsd as fallback; document the choice. Fixtures: hand-pack avcC with a 1920x1088 SPS + crop_bottom 4 (-> 1920x1080) and a pasp 4:3 / tkhd 1440 case.\"},\n {\"id\":\"video-device-provenance\",\"concept\":\"Claimed recording device / producer of a video (make, model, software, encoder, screen recording)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"D18 flavor 'the recording that could not have come from the claimed device'. fmt media (+video/av/mp4/mov). Sources: QuickTime mdta keys/ilst (`com.apple.quicktime.make`, `.model`, `.software`, `.creationdate`, `.location.ISO6709`, `.camera.lens_model`), udta `©mak`/`©mod`/`©swr`/`©too`/`©xyz`/`©day` (2-byte len + 2-byte lang + text), Android `com.android.version`/`com.android.manufacturer`/`com.android.model`/`com.android.capture.fps`, Samsung `smta`/`SEFT`, GoPro `GPMF`/udta `FIRM`, MKV Tags/Info MuxingApp+WritingApp, AVI `ISFT`. Fields: device_make, device_model, device_software, tag_<key> for every mdta key (ffprobe prints mdta keys verbatim as tag names, e.g. `com.apple.quicktime.make`), handler_name (per stream; `Core Media Video` Apple, `VideoHandle` Android, `VideoHandler` Lavf, `ISO Media file produced by Google Inc.`), encoder (stream `encoder` from stsd compressorname Pascal string @entry+50 len<=31, e.g. `Lavc libx264`, `H.264`, `AVC Coding`; container `encoder` from ©too e.g. `Lavf61.1.100`), is_screen_recording heuristics as diagnostics only (no device keys + display-sized odd dims like 886x1920 / 1170x2532 + VFR stts). Answer verbatim strings; absent -> none. Odd-device synthesis goes to video-geometry-synthesis.\"},\n {\"id\":\"video-geometry-synthesis\",\"concept\":\"Cross-file video/image geometry synthesis (originals vs crops, aspect groups, impossible device)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"Extend lib.meta.synthesis (fmt synthesis) over the question's `Files: [...]` (mp4/mov/mkv/jpg/png members; get_bytes per set like digest_order). Dimensions per file = ffprobe width x height (stills included, see media-image-as-video-stream). Fields/ids: dimension_order / pixel_area_order (ascending area, ties by name), largest_frame_file, aspect_ratio_groups (JSON object DAR -> sorted names), original_files (per correlation group the largest frame; group key = title/mdta correlation id `<12 HEX>` tag, else same duration+frame count), cropped_files (smaller than its group original or is_cropped), crop_of (JSON object crop -> original), odd_device_file (claimed make/model disagreeing with the group's majority or geometry/rotation impossible for the claimed device: portrait phone recording with identity matrix and landscape coded size, screen-sized dims with camera make), rotation_groups. Compact JSON, ascending/name order unless the text says otherwise.\"},\n {\"id\":\"video-color-timing\",\"concept\":\"Video color / timing fields (color_*, field_order, has_b_frames, VFR, start_time)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\n  \"detail\":\"fmt media (+video/av). ffprobe names: color_range (`tv`/`pc` from VUI video_full_range_flag or colr nclx full-range bit), color_space (`bt709`, `smpte170m`, `bt2020nc`), color_transfer (`bt709`, `smpte2084`, `arib-std-b67`), color_primaries; field_order (`progressive` when frame_mbs_only_flag, else `tt`/`bb` best-effort), has_b_frames (h264: SPS VUI max_num_reorder_frames else 2 for High with ctts, 0 Baseline), avg_frame_rate (nb_frames / duration reduced) vs r_frame_rate (D18 `10/1`), is_variable_frame_rate (stts deltas differ), start_time (elst media_time / timescale, ffprobe `0.000000`), primary_video_duration (6 decimals), primary_video_bit_rate (btrt avgBitrate else sum(stsz)*8/duration), nb_frames (stsz count; D18 5). Fixtures: D18 mp4 + hand-packed colr box.\"},\n]\nG=G+new\n# order: priority then keep relative\nG.sort(key=lambda g:g['priority'])\nrank_line=\"Ranking (D18 post-run): priority 1 = plausible D19-D21 question with no extractor (or a wrong-answer bug in an existing one), or a harness blocker that silently fails a\\nwhole family of prebuilds. TARGETS-style `fmt`/`fields` given in `detail` for prebuild items.\"\nintro_lines=intro.strip('\\n').split('\\n')\nintro=\"\\n\\n\"+rank_line+\"\\n\\n\"\nout=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g) for g in G)+\"\\n]\\n\"\ns=pre+'## Readiness gaps'+intro+'```json\\n'+out+'```'+after\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\njson.loads(out)\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[g['id'] for g in G if g['action']=='prebuild' and not ((st.get('metadata-forensics:'+g['id']) or {}).get('ok') or (st.get('metadata-forensics:'+g['id']) or {}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(pend),pend)\nprint(len(set(g['id'] for g in G))==len(G))\nE\nsed -n '/^## Readiness gaps/,/```json/p' reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md; tail -c 300 reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md; wc -l reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1138,"cache_read_input_tokens":114405,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1138},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"12ea224e-c03c-442e-a972-e0c7035f8c2a","uuid":"678fde4a-b061-42df-bbcc-361d075ab99e","timestamp":"2026-10-18T13:07:39.704Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9keMxyt9RN3PDZocFJk","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Dx5bNhLcinS3SJnotd6axq":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'E'\nimport json\np='reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md'; s=open(p).read()\npre,rest=s.split('## Readiness gaps',1)\nintro,body=rest.split('```json',1)\njs,after=body.split('```',1)\nG=json.lo