{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9ki5VtqDtc4U6h3Rvj4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I updated both metadata-forensics files and touched nothing else. I ran no tests and made no GM calls.\n\n1. **`reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md`** (220 lines):\n   - **Day 18 entry (\"Frame of Reference\"):**\n     - The field was `media.primary_video_dimensions` = `320x180`, from an h264+aac MP4. The family word is `video` but the fmt word is still `media`.\n     - The prebuilt video extractor in `lib.meta` answered it about 5 s after start.\n     - The single worker added the synthesis handler before the timed runs. Time Trial (23 fields) and Mastery (115) were then CORRECT on the first try, the first clean timed day since D14.\n   - **Other sections:** I updated the overview, the variant axes (field-set size 1/23/115, synthesis members, video size the same in every set), the conventions (video size spelled like JPEG/PNG), a new video row in the cues table, and a new pitfall: four video size sources (sample entry, codec SPS, track header, rotation matrix) can disagree, and ffprobe reports the SPS-cropped size.\n   - I compressed the D1-17 entries to stay near 200 lines.\n\n2. **`reference/coverage/metadata-forensics.md`:**\n   - Added a D18 forecast paragraph and atlas rows 107-112: row 107 marks today's field `seen D18`, the others cover crop/aspect, device provenance, stills read as video, geometry synthesis, and colour/timing.\n   - The cues section now has a video line and is at the 60-line cap.\n   - Dropped the built `media-video-streams` gap.\n\n3. **Readiness gaps:** five new prebuild gaps, so 17 are still unbuilt. Priority 1 starts with **`media-image-as-video-stream`**, a wrong-answer bug I confirmed on the D18 Time Trial kit:\n   - `lib.meta` answers `none` at verified tier when asked `media.primary_video_dimensions` of the kit's JPEG or PNG. ffprobe treats a still image as one video stream, so `none` would be wrong.\n   - It returns nothing at all for the audio-only WAV, where the answer should be the literal `none`.\n\n   It is followed by `video-geometry-crop-aspect`, `video-device-provenance`, `mp4-mov-atoms` and `video-geometry-synthesis`. I lowered the other-audio-containers gap (ASF/AIFF/CAF) to priority 2."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1344,"cache_read_input_tokens":120326,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1344},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"12ea224e-c03c-442e-a972-e0c7035f8c2a","uuid":"9410e88e-be9b-48fd-9d9c-f0b47efdc262","timestamp":"2026-10-18T13:07:59.500Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9ki575hD9K9YkKfsRhW"}
